AC Electrical Circuit Analysis — James M. Fiore (@pe-fiore-ac: 0, is #reference, #part-of @pe-sources) { r_0C4FYP5P0A5GQP13HAD8FTEEWK
James M. Fiore. AC Electrical Circuit Analysis: A Practical Approach. [Author](https://www.jimfiore.org/Books.html) · [Complete author PDF](https://www.jimfiore.org/books/ACElectricalCircuitAnalysis.pdf) · [Milne publisher record and lab manual](https://milneopentextbooks.org/ac-electrical-circuit-analysis-a-practical-approach/).

Read the whole book after the DC foundation: sinusoids, complex quantities, RLC networks, network theorems, nodal/mesh methods, AC power, resonance, polyphase systems and frequency response. Work substantial problems and the appropriate full laboratory studies. Keep RMS/peak and time-sign conventions explicit when comparing with the shared field notes.

Milne lists publication 17 February 2021 and CC BY-NC-SA; the author's collection links the 3.0 Unported licence. Preserve the actual edition's terms, distinct from a website footer. The current author-file retrieval reported 422 file pages on 29 October 2026; subsequent text requests timed out. Contents were checked through the publisher, not by inspecting every page of that revised PDF. All files remain external references.

**Return:** [Power-engineering sources — complete books, courses, methods and evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_12EFX00X7ZXGT9MPMJDYRTNY9N).
